Tricky Interview Question of DevOps :

What Happened if POD received more traffic/load than its limit? ( Where Auto scale is not configured )

Answer:

1. If CPU limit is exceeded
Kubernetes throttles the container:

The app becomes slow / high latency
Requests may start timing out

👉 Example: If CPU limit = 500m and traffic spikes → container can’t use more → performance drops

 2. If the memory limit is exceeded:

Kubernetes triggers OOMKilled (Out Of Memory)
Container is killed and restarted

👉 This is dangerous for:
APIs (downtime)
Stateful apps (data loss risk).
